I want these notes to document not only what I changed, but also what I was thinking at the time, what I expected to happen, what actually happened, and what I learned from being wrong.

What's Next?

The Guessing Game is the first major project inside the larger RL Playground.

The next stage is to formalize the experimentation around it: testing how different strategies respond to changes in search-space complexity, state representation, feature distributions, and other environmental properties.

The longer-term goal is for this project to become a place where I can experiment with Reinforcement Learning ideas rather than simply implement them.

Some experiments may succeed.

Some may fail.

Both are useful.

The point of the playground is to build something, watch what happens, and understand why.